# Dann's routing brain — a named Ollama model built from qwen2.5:7b-instruct,
# chosen over llama3.2:3b for stronger structured tool-call/function
# selection. Build/rebuild with scripts/build_router_model.sh, or directly:
#   ollama create dann-router -f models/dann-router.Modelfile
#
# What this file can and can't control: every real Dann request (voice via
# src/orchestrator.py, text via app/services/chat_service.py) sends its own
# "system" message (the live AGENTS section compiled from config.yaml's
# agents: list — see src/agents_config.py) and its own temperature/num_predict
# in the request "options". Both override anything set below for that
# request. So the SYSTEM prompt here is only a fallback for standalone
# testing (`ollama run dann-router "..."`), and temperature/max_tokens tuning
# belongs in config.yaml's ollama.temperature/max_tokens, not here.
#
# What IS only set here, because the orchestrator never sends it per-request:
# num_ctx, top_p, repeat_penalty.

FROM qwen2.5:7b-instruct

# Ollama's runtime context window defaults to 2048 regardless of a model's
# max context, silently truncating older turns/tool schemas once the AGENTS
# section + all currently-registered MCP tool schemas + conversation history
# grow past that. 8192 comfortably covers Dann's current tool set with room
# to add more agents before this needs raising.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# Modest determinism boost for tool-call selection, since this isn't sent
# per-request the way temperature is.
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# Safety cap for standalone testing (`ollama run dann-router "..."`), where
# no per-request max_tokens is sent. Real requests always override this with
# config.yaml's ollama.max_tokens.
PARAMETER num_predict 200

SYSTEM """
You are Dann, a voice/text assistant with a routing brain: for every
request, decide whether to answer directly or call a tool, based on the
AGENTS list you're given each turn. Never call a tool for conversational
filler. After a tool call, speak the result naturally in 1-2 sentences and
stop. Never use markdown, lists, or code formatting in your own responses.
"""
